+### `cleanDoubleSlashes(input, options?)`
 
 Removes double slashes from the URL.
 
+If `options.respectQueryAndFragment` is `true`, only the part before the query (`?`) and fragment (`#`) is cleaned and the rest is left untouched.
+
 **Example:**
 
 ```js
@@ -225,6 +227,9 @@ cleanDoubleSlashes("//foo//bar//"); // "/foo/bar/"
 
 cleanDoubleSlashes("http://example.com/analyze//http://localhost:3000//");
 // Returns "http://example.com/analyze/http://localhost:3000/"
+
+cleanDoubleSlashes("/foo//bar?redirect=//baz", { respectQueryAndFragment: true });
+// Returns "/foo/bar?redirect=//baz"
 ```
 
